WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.240
Researchers combine nearly 3,500 airborne LiDAR surveys into the first consistent global three-dimensional map of forest canopies spanning 56 countries. This is Planetterrian Daily, episode 257. After the atlas come oxygen and lifespan in a mitochondrial disease model, leisure versus labor for dementia risk, and a science deep dive on why movement context matters. A University of Bristol-led group in a Fizz.org account of a Nature Ecology and Evolution paper.

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:34.480
However, spent five years covering more than 5.5 million hectares with airplanes, helicopters,

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:35.360
and drones.

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:40.460
Those flights produced matched maps of canopy height and terrain elevation, rather than

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:42.460
a patchwork of incompatible surveys.

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:48.680
Almost 20% of the surveyed area carries repeated measurements, so the same stands can be compared

00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:49.420
across time.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:57.040
Researchers at more than 100 institutions contributed scenes spanning 224 ecological regions, and a public

00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:01.400
website and archive let users find flights by location, date, and collector.

00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:07.720
The maps feed carbon stock estimates, biodiversity monitoring, and checks on satellite systems

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:10.900
including the European Space Agency's Biomass mission.

00:01:11.915 --> 00:01:18.375
Defective H-T-R-A2 protein impairs mitochondrial complex-1 and lets oxygen build to toxic levels

00:01:18.375 --> 00:01:23.035
and brain tissue, according to science daily coverage of Gladstone Institute's work.

00:01:23.035 --> 00:01:28.075
Mark, mice lacking that protein that breathed reduced oxygen air lived three times longer

00:01:28.075 --> 00:01:31.815
than litter mates in normal air and showed less striatal inflammation.

00:01:32.455 --> 00:01:38.635
The team traced HTRA-2 to a cleanup partnership with CLPB that keeps misfolded proteins

00:01:38.635 --> 00:01:40.175
from clogging complex-1.

00:01:40.815 --> 00:01:46.015
The same genetic screen flag 75 other disease-linked genes that might respond to hypoxia.

00:01:46.695 --> 00:01:49.735
Postdoctoral fellow anchor Garg led the mouse experiments.

00:01:49.735 --> 00:01:55.194
Natan Fetter at the University of Southern California led an analysis of how different

00:01:55.194 --> 00:01:57.954
kinds of physical activity track with later dementia.

00:01:58.454 --> 00:02:05.014
74 studies covering more than 4.2 million adults linked recreational exercise to 24% lower

00:02:05.014 --> 00:02:06.534
all-cause dementia risk.

00:02:07.154 --> 00:02:12.294
Physically demanding work correlated with 20% higher risk after a median 10-year follow-up.

00:02:12.894 --> 00:02:16.114
Household chores showed benefit in the single study that measured them.

00:02:16.114 --> 00:02:22.074
The pattern held for Alzheimer's and vascular dementia and was non-linear, risk fell as leisure

00:02:22.074 --> 00:02:26.754
activity rose, and it rose with more occupational activity before plateauing.

00:02:27.254 --> 00:02:31.594
Fetter pointed to social and environmental factors around work as the likely drivers

00:02:31.594 --> 00:02:32.334
of that split.

00:02:33.269 --> 00:02:37.409
Something most people get wrong is the belief that the brain treats every kind of physical

00:02:37.409 --> 00:02:39.329
movement as the same protective dose.

00:02:40.029 --> 00:02:45.089
Chosen recreational effort usually arrives at an intensity the person picks, with rest

00:02:45.089 --> 00:02:47.969
Just built into the weak and with other people around the activity.

00:02:48.489 --> 00:02:52.749
The body works, then it recovers, and that cycle is part of the session rather than

00:02:52.749 --> 00:02:53.309
an accident.

00:02:54.189 --> 00:02:59.149
Occupational labor often repeats the same strain, cuts rest short, and stacks workplace

00:02:59.149 --> 00:03:01.389
stressors across years instead of hours.

00:03:02.069 --> 00:03:04.489
Those conditions do not cancel the fact of movement.

00:03:05.069 --> 00:03:07.509
They change what the movement does while it is happening.

00:03:08.169 --> 00:03:12.869
Social contact around leisure can sit beside the effort, whereas job demands can isolate

00:03:12.869 --> 00:03:17.529
the same muscles inside noise, heat, time pressure, or limited control.

00:03:18.189 --> 00:03:21.969
Chronic strain without recovery is a different exposure from a hike that ends.

00:03:22.589 --> 00:03:27.029
Scheduled, self-paced activity is the form the review ties to brain health gains,

00:03:27.529 --> 00:03:30.529
rather than assuming job demands will do that work on their own.

00:03:31.109 --> 00:03:35.989
The next decisive measurement is whether adding protected recovery time to physically demanding jobs

00:03:35.989 --> 00:03:39.209
narrows the gap already observed between leisure and labor.

00:03:39.209 --> 00:03:46.332
chemists at Virginia Tech placed common polyvinyl chloride or PVC from pipes, frames, and

00:03:46.332 --> 00:03:51.532
cards into solvent with aluminum trichloride and alpha olephins. The mixture heated to

00:03:51.532 --> 00:03:58.092
158 degrees Fahrenheit for three hours and yielded poly-alpha olephin, a stable synthetic lubricant

00:03:58.092 --> 00:04:03.572
base stock. The root up cycles material that resist ordinary recycling because of its chlorine

00:04:03.572 --> 00:04:09.192
content and additives. Earlier work from the same lab turned other plastics into surfactants

00:04:09.192 --> 00:04:14.992
used in soaps. The resulting oil belongs to a family valued for stability across wide temperature

00:04:14.992 --> 00:04:21.615
ranges. Tahora Samad and senior author Sanghita Bhattia at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology

00:04:21.615 --> 00:04:28.455
or MIT attached the cancer-approved antibiotic Kellitchie-Maisin to Albuiman and paired it with

00:04:28.455 --> 00:04:32.375
circulating antidote protein, work described by MIT Health.

00:04:32.695 --> 00:04:38.095
The conjugate is cleaved only by neutrophil elastase at infection sites, and the antidote

00:04:38.095 --> 00:04:40.455
stays in circulation to further shield the liver.

00:04:41.015 --> 00:04:45.655
In mice, the modified compound cleared bacterial pneumonia with lower liver damage than

00:04:45.655 --> 00:04:46.335
the free drug.

00:04:46.955 --> 00:04:52.155
Reusing a molecule whose oncology safety data already exists shortens the path toward antibiotic

00:04:52.155 --> 00:04:52.815
development.

00:04:52.815 --> 00:04:59.173
A naturally released exercise molecule improved force generation, delayed fatigue and protected

00:04:59.173 --> 00:05:01.173
against damage in laboratory tests.

00:05:01.773 --> 00:05:06.453
The compound is already sold as a dietary supplement and is being examined for muscle

00:05:06.453 --> 00:05:08.213
loss tied to type 2 diabetes.

00:05:09.299 --> 00:05:13.599
Greater screen time and infancy and in the early school years tracked with poorer working

00:05:13.599 --> 00:05:16.539
memory and weaker school performance measured years later.

00:05:17.119 --> 00:05:22.319
Harvard engineers built a microscopic chip that converts red light into ultraviolet at 120

00:05:22.319 --> 00:05:27.599
times typical output, at efficiencies that could shrink quantum computers, atomic clocks,

00:05:27.899 --> 00:05:32.519
and environmental sensors. University of Auckland researchers identified structural

00:05:32.519 --> 00:05:37.459
features in sharp cartilage that may be copied into biomaterials without harvesting the animals.

00:05:38.139 --> 00:05:42.919
Direct brain recordings reported in Nature showed that Warnocki's area takes part in a cognitive

00:05:42.919 --> 00:05:49.199
step that precedes articulation, beyond word recognition alone. Structural work on a disease-linked

00:05:49.199 --> 00:05:53.579
protein revealed two distinct mechanisms that govern how the transporter selects amino

00:05:53.579 --> 00:05:56.659
acid substrates and moves them across membranes.

00:05:57.219 --> 00:06:04.579
St. Jude researchers mapped how type IF3 CRISPR-associated transposes, or CAST, complexes

00:06:04.579 --> 00:06:10.319
choose target sites, then redesigned a protein to raise DNA insertion precision and insertion

00:06:10.319 --> 00:06:10.819
activity.

00:06:11.399 --> 00:06:16.819
In short, many women see eating disorder symptoms intensify before and after childbirth, yet

00:06:16.819 --> 00:06:22.099
received no targeted screening, a gap STAT news called a perfect storm that clinicians

00:06:22.099 --> 00:06:22.979
often miss.

00:06:23.499 --> 00:06:28.959
An EIT food study found European consumers weigh health, taste, cost, and convenience

00:06:28.959 --> 00:06:34.079
more heavily than novelty or sustainability claims when they judge food biotechnology.

